s.t:
The qualified nursing assistant, within the care team, participates in the overall care of the resident by providing basic care (hygiene, feeding) and assisting the referring nurse in carrying out care. He/she ensures the comfort and well-being of the resident by supporting them in their daily life activities.
He/she collaborates with all professionals from the various EMS services in an interdisciplinary manner. The qualified nursing assistant must be able to work as part of a team and demonstrate tact, discretion, respect, listening skills and empathy towards residents and their families.
Profile sought
* ASA nursing assistant training (mandatory); Care delegation training is an asset
* Minimum 3-5 years experience in a similar position within an EMS in Switzerland (an asset);
* Good listening skills and interpersonal skills;
* Good understanding of the needs of elderly people;
* Aptitude to work in an interdisciplinary team and independently;
* Good prioritisation skills and sense of observation;
* Good knowledge of French and ability to convey written information;
* Knowledge of IT tools and care software (SIEMS an asset).
Application procedures and address

* Recevoir les appels téléphoniques, analyser les demandes, au besoin et avec l'avis du ou de la médecin, fixer les rendez-vous ;
* Accueillir les patients, les installer, les rassurer, les aider à se préparer pour les divers examens prévus ;
* Réaliser divers soins tels que les pansements, les prises de sang et injections ;
* Assister le médecin lors de petites chirurgies ;
* Réaliser sur demande, divers examens tels que des électrocardiogrammes et des radiographies ;
* Procéder à diverses analyses de chimie sèche, d'hématologie et tests rapides.
